import"./chunk-GAL4ENT6.js";var s="# NgRx SignalStore\n\nA contest entry. State is held in NgRx SignalStore (`withState`, `withEntities`,\n`withMethods`, `withComputed`, `rxMethod`), not in another approach's RxJS\nclasses. Loaders are the API services, which are Observables; the cache\naround them is the store's own. Judged by the page tests\n(`PAGE_TARGET=signal-store npm test`) and the e2e suite\n(`E2E_CONTESTER=signal-store npm run e2e`).\n\nStatus: see [test_report.md](test_report.md), regenerated by `npm run test:report`.\nThe tool's gaps for this page are in [gaps.md](gaps.md).\n\n## Extra code\n\nCode that is not about the page's domain: caches, batching, status mapping,\nlifetime, written per entity or as generic helpers. Lines from\n[card 06](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/06-boilerplate.md) (Prettier-formatted, non-blank, non-comment), compared with\nthe four entries (vanilla-rxjs, ngrx-signal-store, resources,\nstateful-observable).\n\n| Measure | Lines | vs average | vs best | vs worst |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Extra code (generic + per-entity) | **416** | +7% vs average (388) | +227 vs best | \u2212179 vs worst |\n| Whole data layer | **618** | \u221226% vs average (840) | +317 vs best | \u22121050 vs worst |\n| One more batched lookup like `tiers` | **14** | \u221227% vs average (19) | +1 vs best | \u221216 vs worst |\n\nThe lookup cost has no batching, which this entry does not meet (R-L9): with it, the number would be higher.\n\n## Idea\n\nEvery fetched entity (customer, orders, tiers, prices, ...) is one\n`createKeyedCache` (`data/entity-store.ts`): a `signalStore` with\n\n- `withEntities`: one slot per id, so every reader of the same id reads the\n  same signal (R-L10);\n- `attach(id)` / `detach(id)`: a reference count per id. The first attach\n  starts the load; the last detach cancels a load still in flight and keeps a\n  settled value;\n- `reload(id)`, `set(id, value)`, `clear()`: Retry and polls, a write's\n  result, and logout;\n- `peek`, a `withComputed` read that is pure and safe inside `computed()`.\n\nA view reads a key with `cacheEntry(cache, idSignal)`, which runs an\n`effect()` that attaches the current id and detaches it in the cleanup. The\nread itself is `peek`, because Angular forbids writing signals inside\n`computed()`.\n\nThe customer list's filter, sort and page are a second, small store:\n`UI_STATE` (`data/ui-state.ts`) holds named fields with `withState`,\n`withMethods` and `patchState`. Its search text is typed into `typedText` at\nonce and debounced into `query.text` by an `rxMethod`.\n\nField components (`ProductName`, `CustomerTier`, `Kpi`, ...) each inject the\ncache for their own value and take their own id as an input. No lookup comes\nfrom a parent.\n\n## Good\n\n- A keyed read is one line in a field: `cacheEntry(this.cache, this.sku)`.\n  The state (`loading`, `ready`, `reloading`, `error`) comes with it.\n- One slot per id gives sharing for free: the list row, the header and the tab\n  badge of one customer read the same tier entry (R-L10, R-J7).\n- Typing is debounced by `rxMethod` in the customer list (R-L4), and the\n  store's `withMethods` keeps each write next to the state it changes.\n- Logout clears the user-bound caches in one call (`Auth.signOut`), and\n  products, prices, stock and the product search are not in that list, so\n  they survive it (R-L6, R-S4).\n\n## Bad\n\nOnly failing requirements and the excess code they cost (spec \xA711). All three\nare the tool's gaps G1 and G2, explained in [gaps.md](gaps.md).\n\n- **Batching is not met** (R-L9; G2 in `gaps.md`). `tiers`, `ticketCounts` and\n  `prices` go out one id per call: `A2`, `C11` (8 calls each for one list\n  page), `C7`, `B10` (one `prices` call per hit), `C12` (24 `prices` calls for\n  a 24-line cart, 2 expected), `D7` (one release shows only the first hit's\n  price). The store has no batching primitive; meeting it means a per-tick\n  buffer with chunks and per-id errors (vanilla's `entity-cache.ts`, 136\n  lines) inside `createKeyedCache`.\n- **The keyed async cache is hand-written** (R-L3, R-L5, R-L10, R-C4; G1 in\n  `gaps.md`). `@ngrx/signals` holds state but does not load it.\n  `createKeyedCache` and its readers (`entity-store.ts`, 132 lines) keep two\n  `Map`s (observers and in-flight `Subject` per id) next to `withEntities`.\n  The same job as vanilla's `Query`, but here every scenario it serves passes.\n- **`untracked()` and the `peek`/`attach` split are a workaround.**\n  `cacheEntry` wraps its attach and detach in `untracked()`: without it their\n  signal reads become effect dependencies and a failed id retries forever.\n  The split exists because `computed()` cannot write.\n\n## Requirements\n\n| Requirement | How it is met |\n| --- | --- |\n| R-S1 | helper: `signedIn` in `data/ui-state.ts`; the page's `@if` shows only the sign-in screen |\n| R-S2 | helper: a section's `cacheEntry` attaches its keys when the section is created |\n| R-S3 | helper: `Auth.signOut` clears the session caches and the signed-in flag at once (`data/auth.ts`) |\n| R-S4 | helper: `clear()` drops values and slots of every user-bound cache (`entity-store.ts`) |\n| R-S5 | helper: the last tab is a root signal in `UI_STATE`; the customer and panel are not kept |\n| R-D1 | helper: each keyed section reads its own cache entry (`cacheEntry`) |\n| R-D2 | helper: `poll()` in `entity-store.ts` reloads on an interval while its section lives |\n| R-B1 | helper: `app-view-block` takes `loading` and `error` from `data/block-state.ts` |\n| R-J1 | helper: field components read their own entry; nothing unresolved is an empty value |\n| R-J2 | helper: each field reads the entry for its own id (name, price, stock, tier) |\n| R-J3 | helper: the batch endpoints are called one id per call (`sources.ts`), so the limit holds trivially; batching itself is not met (R-L9) |\n| R-J4 | helper: cart lines and hits read the `PRICE` entry of their sku |\n| R-J5 | helper: the linked ticket is read from `TICKETS_BY_ORDER` (`data/mappers.ts`) |\n| R-J6 | not in the data layer: sentences are written by the shared views |\n| R-J7 | helper: each counter has one owner entry (`ORDER_STATS`, `TICKET_COUNT`, `TIER`) |\n| R-C1 | helper: `cacheEntry`'s effect cleanup detaches the previous id when the input changes |\n| R-C2 | helper: `peek` returns loading for the new key, so the block shows loading, not the old data |\n| R-W1 | helper: `createAction` (`data/action.ts`) publishes `pending` and `error` to the control |\n| R-W2 | helper: the control is disabled while the action is pending |\n| R-W3 | helper: `onSave` reloads every affected entry after success (`order-panel-section`) |\n| R-W5 | helper: `Auth.signOut` clears the caches, so a result from an earlier session is not shown |\n| R-W6 | not in the data layer: the shared order view offers Create return |\n| R-W7 | not used: no optimistic display |\n| R-B2 | helper: `app-view-block` replaces the spinner block in every section |\n| R-E1 | helper: a failed source shows its error where its data would be (`block-state.ts`, `fieldError`) |\n| R-E2 | built in: an entry in `error` is attached again by the next observer (`attach` checks the status) |\n| R-E3 | helper: `createAction` keeps the user's input on failure |\n| R-G1 | helper: `error(state)` in `block-state.ts` names the failed source |\n| R-G2 | helper: the block's text is `Couldn't load <source>` from the failed key |\n| R-G3 | helper: each field entry fails on its own; `fieldError` keeps the rest of the section |\n| R-G4 | helper: `run()` keeps the last value when a reload fails; `poll` keeps polling |\n| R-G5 | helper: Retry calls `reload(id)` for the failed key only |\n| R-G6 | helper: fields degrade in place; the cart total and the hit Add show their own error with Reload |\n| R-C3 | helper: a reload keeps the value and sets `reloading` (`fetched.reloading`) |\n| R-C4 | helper: `detach` cancels the in-flight load with `takeUntil` on a per-id `Subject` (`entity-store.ts`) |\n| R-W8 | helper: a write is an action outside the section's cache entries, so navigation does not cancel it |\n| R-W9 | helper: `createAction` keeps the input on error |\n| R-W10 | helper: `onSave` reloads the affected orders, stats, stock and ticket entries |\n| R-L1 | helper: `Auth.signOut` clears the caches and the polls stop with their sections |\n| R-L2 | helper: `attach` runs only when a visible section's effect runs |\n| R-L3 | helper: one slot per id plus the observer count in `entity-store.ts` |\n| R-L4 | helper: `typeSearch` (`rxMethod`) debounces the customer list; the order editor debounces with `toObservable` and `debounce` |\n| R-L11 | helper: sentence names are their own entries (`CUSTOMER`, `AGENT_NAME`), read only when a row shows them |\n| R-L9 | **not met**: one id per call for `tiers`, `ticketCounts`, `prices` (see Bad and gaps.md) |\n| R-L10 | built in: `withEntities` gives one signal per id, read by every reader |\n| R-L5 | helper: a settled value stays in `values` after the last detach |\n| R-L6 | helper: `SEARCH_PRODUCTS`, `PRICE`, `STOCK` are not in `SESSION_CACHES` |\n| R-L7 | helper: `reload(id)` on the entries a write changes |\n| R-L8 | helper: `poll()` runs only while its section exists (`destroyRef`) |\n| R-P1 | built in: independent entries are independent signals; each section renders on its own |\n| R-P2 | helper: the in-flight orders list is its own entry, and each row reads its own shipment |\n| R-P3 | helper: the order and its names are separate entries (`ORDER`, `PRODUCT_NAME`) |\n| R-P4 | helper: a dependent key starts when its id signal is set (`cacheEntry` effect) |\n| R-P5 | helper: `cacheEntryOptional` asks nothing while its key is `null` |\n| R-P6 | helper: each cart line's price is its own entry (`cacheEntries`) |\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\nEight criteria, the same in every entry's README. Each is compared across the entries in [docs/contest/results](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/criteria.md); the numbers below come from there (line counts: card [06](https://github.com/earthdmitriy/rx-evo/blob/master/docs/contest/results/06-boilerplate.md), Prettier-formatted, non-blank, non-comment).\n\n- **Eager or lazy start.** Lazy. `cacheEntry` attaches its id from an `effect()`, which runs when the section that reads it is created (`data/entity-store.ts`). Gives: a hidden section asks nothing. Costs: the start goes through an `effect()` with `untracked()` attach/detach, kept right by hand.\n- **One request per key, and how long a value lives.** `withEntities` gives one slot per id; an observer count per id decides when to start and when to stop. Values live until `clear()` on logout (`Auth.signOut`, `data/sources.ts` `SESSION_CACHES`). No eviction. Gives: one request per key. Costs: the count and the map of observers are written by hand.\n- **Cancelling a superseded read.** The last `detach` cancels an in-flight load through a per-id `Subject` and `takeUntil` (`entity-store.ts`). Gives: a superseded answer is dropped. Costs: one more map of in-flight subjects to keep in step with the slots.\n- **Batching.** None: each id is one call. Costs: the batch endpoints fail R-L9 (`gaps.md`); a batch would be new code on top of the store.\n- **Keeping data on error or reload.** `reload()` sets `reloading` and keeps the value; a failed load sets `error` and keeps the last value (`fetched.error(value)`). Gives: the value is kept on purpose. Costs: every field needs its own error branch, `fieldError` in `data/block-state.ts`.\n- **Boilerplate to add one value.** One more batched lookup like `tiers` costs 14 lines in 3 files (without batching, which is not met). The data layer is 618 lines: 259 generic, 157 per entity, 202 domain. Costs: a value must also be listed in `SESSION_CACHES` or logout keeps it.\n- **Where state lives.** Values in root stores (`sources.ts`); UI state in one root store (`UI_STATE`). Gives: a value outlives the component that read it. Costs: root stores must be cleared on logout by hand (`Auth.signOut`).\n- **Dependency on a library.** `@ngrx/signals`, plus RxJS for the loaders. Gives: the store's own primitives. Costs: the store API is the library's, so upgrades follow its changes.\n\n## Try it\n\n- Select different customers: the header, the tab badges and the list row all\n  read the same tier entry; switch away and back and nothing refetches.\n- Filter or sort the customer list: the query is held in `UI_STATE`, and a\n  change to it reads a new key.\n- Turn on **Throw** on any service in the request panel above the demo: the\n  section fails in isolation, and its fields show an error with Reload.\n- Open the Cart tab, leave the page and come back: the tab is remembered\n  (R-S5); the customer and the open panel are not.\n";export{s as default};
